      "description": "Search Page View All Jobs Human Resources My Benefits Why Colorado College Applicant Login Kiosk mode Ignite Your Passion, Unleash Your Potential Skip to jobs search results Clear Filters Category Search categories 12 filter options found Category Athletics (4 items) 4 Campus Safety & Security (2 items) 2 Communications & Marketing (1 items) 1 Dean of Faculty (2 items) 2 Dean of the College (1 items) 1 Faculty - Humanities (2 items) 2 Faculty - Natural Sciences (3 items) 3 Faculty - Social Sciences (2 items) 2 Finance & Administration (1 items) 1 Fine Arts Center (1 items) 1 Human Resources (1 items) 1 Information Technology (1 items) 1 Employment Type Search employment types 3 filter options found Employment Type Faculty - Tenure Track (7 items) 7 Staff - Full Time (10 items) 10 Staff - Other (Temporary or Occasional) (4 items) 4 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Sort by: Last Updated Last Updated: Newest to Oldest Last Updated: Oldest to Newest Title: A-Z Title: Z-A Assistant Athletic Trainer On Campus Athletics Staff - Full Time About Us: Colorado College (“CC”) is a private, four-year, highly selective liberal arts college of 2,100 undergraduate students and a small Master of Arts in teaching program. It is located on a 99-acre campus adjacent to downtown, ‘Olympic City’, Colorado Springs. The campus sits on the Front Range of the Rocky Mountains at the foot of Pikes Peak. The college operates an innovative curricular approach, known as the Block Plan, which entails students taking one course at a time for three and a half weeks, with the academic year divided into eight “blocks.” The Colorado College Department of Athletics sponsors 17 varsity programs. Fifteen programs compete at the NCAA Division III level and two at the Division I level. Division III programs are members of the Southern Collegiate Athletic Conference (SCAC), with the exception of Men’s Lacrosse (independent) and Women’s Lacrosse (WIAC affiliate). Division I Men’s Hockey is a member of the National Collegiate Hockey Conference (NCHC) and Division I Women’s Soccer competes as an affiliate member of the Mountain West Conference (MWC).  \n\nThe purpose of this role is to provide education, independent health care, and preventative services for our varsity student-athletes, coaching staff, and members of the Athletic Department.  Work closely with other full-time athletic trainers, physical therapist, and the athletic insurance coordinator to assist in the day-to-day management of the athletic department’s intercollegiate sports medicine operation and provide effective delivery of athletic training services. Read more Assistant Professor of Film and Media Studies On Campus Faculty - Humanities Faculty - Tenure Track Closing on: Dec 30 2026 Assistant Professor of Film and Media Studies Read more Accounts Payable Specialist On Campus Finance & Administration Staff - Full Time Closing on: Sep 20 2026 The Accounts Payable Specialist supports the College's financial operations through the accurate, timely, and compliant processing of accounts payable transactions. This role serves as a key resource for purchasing, P-Card administration, vendor management, payment processes, and customer service while supporting strong internal controls and effective financial stewardship. Responsibilities within these functional areas may be assigned, redistributed, or shared among team members based on business needs, workload, staffing levels, and individual expertise. Read more Classroom Systems and Events Technician On Campus Information Technology Staff - Full Time Closing on: Sep 20 2026 Join Colorado College as the Classroom Systems and Events Technician, where you'll play a key role in delivering exceptional classroom technology support and event experiences that enhance teaching, learning, and campus engagement. The purpose of this role is to provide AV technical support for 190+ smart classrooms and learning spaces; perform lifecycle replacements of AV technology in these rooms as well as ongoing preventive maintenance and repairs; and provide professional technical support for events, meetings, and conferences requiring audio visual technology. Read more Executive Writer & Editor On Campus Communications & Marketing Staff - Full Time The Executive Writer & Editor plays a central role in shaping Colorado College’s voice through high-quality, high-impact content that supports institutional priorities and elevates executive and College visibility. Reporting to the Director of Institutional Communications, this position is responsible for writing, editing, and editorial strategy support across executive communications, internal messaging, public relations, marketing, and campus-wide content needs. This includes serving as the principle writer for presidential and executive remarks as well as supporting communications on major initiatives and providing editorial services and style oversight in alignment with college brand messaging. \n\nThe role is both strategic and executional, requiring exceptional writing, editorial judgment, and collaboration to ensure communications are clear, compelling, and aligned with the college’s voice and values. Read more Assistant Professor of Organismal Biology & Ecology On Campus Faculty - Natural Sciences Faculty - Tenure Track Closing on: Sep 16 2026 Assistant Professor of Organismal Biology & Ecology Read more Assistant Professor of Philosophy On Campus Faculty - Humanities Faculty - Tenure Track Closing on: Oct 5 2026 Assistant Professor of Philosophy Read more Associate Athletic Director for Compliance, Student-Athlete Success & Operations On Campus Athletics Staff - Full Time About Us: Colorado College (“CC”) is a private, four-year, highly selective liberal arts college of 2,100 undergraduate students and a small Master of Arts in teaching program. It is located on a 99-acre campus adjacent to downtown, ‘Olympic City’, Colorado Springs. The campus sits on the Front Range of the Rocky Mountains at the foot of Pikes Peak. The college operates an innovative curricular approach, known as the Block Plan, which entails students taking one course at a time for three and a half weeks, with the academic year divided into eight “blocks.” The Colorado College Department of Athletics sponsors 17 varsity programs. Fifteen programs compete at the NCAA Division III level and two at the Division I level. Division III programs are members of the Southern Collegiate Athletic Conference (SCAC), with the exception of Men’s Lacrosse (independent) and Women’s Lacrosse (WIAC affiliate). Division I Men’s Hockey is a member of the National Collegiate Hockey Conference (NCHC) and Division I Women’s Soccer competes as an affiliate member of the Mountain West Conference (MWC).   \n\nOversees the NCAA compliance approach for a highly competitive multi-division institution. Plans for, directs and enforces the division’s compliance with NCAA, conference, and college rules and regulations and oversees the coordination and implementation of a holistic student-athlete support program including coordinating on campus resources and strategies conducive to the academic, athletic and personal development of the student-athletes. \n\nPrimary responsibilities include but are not limited to strategic and day-to-day management of NCAA compliance (Division I and Division III), oversight and management of the division’s student-athlete services program, liaison to key campus offices, sport oversight, and support of areas including events, facilities and budget management. Read more Academic Administrative Assistant On Campus Dean of Faculty Staff - Full Time Closing on: Sep 23 2026 Play a vital role in supporting the Department of Economics & Business as our Academic Administrative Assistant. In this position, you will partner closely with the department chair, faculty, and staff to support teaching, research, and day-to-day operations. You’ll help keep the department running smoothly by managing business and administrative functions, ensuring efficiency and strong operational practices. As a key point of contact, you will connect with students, campus partners, and the broader community—helping create a responsive, organized, and welcoming environment. Read more Assistant Professor of Psychology and Neuroscience On Campus Faculty - Natural Sciences Faculty - Tenure Track Closing on: Oct 16 2026 Assistant Professor of Psychology and Neuroscience Read more Campus Safety Officer On Campus Campus Safety & Security Staff - Full Time Join Colorado College as a Campus Safety Officer and help foster a safe, welcoming, and secure campus community. In this highly visible role, you will support campus safety through patrol, emergency response, community engagement, and daily communication operations. Working closely with students, faculty, staff, and visitors, you will promote awareness of campus resources and College policies while helping protect the people, property, and reputation of Colorado College. As part of a 24/7 operation, Campus Safety Officers may be assigned to weekends, holidays, overnight shifts, and critical incident response, playing an essential role in maintaining a safe learning and living environment for all. Read more Assistant Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry On Campus Faculty - Natural Sciences Faculty - Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry Read more Occasional Arena Operations/Ice Technician On Campus Athletics Staff - Other (Temporary or Occasional) Serves an integral role to the daily operation of Ed Robson Arena and is responsible for the day-to-day facility operations of the Arena to include Zamboni operation, building upkeep/repairs, cleanliness, functionality of equipment and arena setup/strike. Read more Assistant Professor of Political Science On Campus Faculty - Social Sciences Faculty - Tenure Track Closing on: Sep 8 2026 Assistant Professor of Political Science Read more Technical Director On Campus Dean of Faculty Staff - Full Time Closing on: Sep 14 2026 The Technical Director is responsible for ensuring the effective operation, maintenance, and support of the Geology Department’s laboratories, field equipment, instrumentation, and computing resources and works closely with faculty to support teaching, research, and field-based learning activities. This position oversees a diverse array of specialized scientific and instructional equipment (see full list at https://www.coloradocollege.edu/academics/dept/geology/about-us/facilities.html). Read more Assistant Professor of Economics and Business On Campus Faculty - Social Sciences Faculty - Tenure Track Closing on: Nov 1 2026 Full-time, tenure-track faculty position in Economics and Business Read more Associate Vice President, Human Resources On Campus Human Resources Staff - Full Time The Associate Vice President for Human Resources (AVP-HR) provides strategic and operational leadership for a comprehensive human resources program at Colorado College, including talent acquisition, total rewards, performance management, leadership and talent development, employee relations, workforce planning, HR technology and analytics, and policy development and compliance. The AVP-HR partners with the Office of Civil\nRights, Institutional Equity and Belonging, and other campus leaders to ensure equity and belonging are embedded throughout HR policy and practice, and that the employee experience reflects the College’s mission and values.\n\nReporting to the Vice President of Finance & Administration/Chief Financial Officer, the AVP-HR serves as a key strategic advisor to the CFO and to senior leadership across the College on workforce strategy and organizational health. Read more OC Campus Safety Officer On Campus Campus Safety & Security Staff - Other (Temporary or Occasional) The Occasional Campus Safety Officer works on an as-needed basis to help maintain a safe and secure campus environment by protecting the lives, property, and reputation of Colorado College and supporting the safety of students, employees, guests, and visitors. Read more Audio Visual Supervisor On Campus Fine Arts Center Staff - Full Time Lead the delivery of exceptional audio-visual experiences as our Audio-Visual Supervisor! Reporting to the Director of Production, this role provides leadership and oversight for all audio-visual needs supporting Fine Arts Center Theatre Company productions. You’ll collaborate closely with visiting designers, artists, and colleagues across the FAC to bring creative visions to life and ensure a high-quality experience for our audiences. This position plays a key role in fostering collaboration, supporting innovation, and upholding the artistic excellence that defines our performances. Read more Occasional Head Coach - Mock Trial Program On Campus Dean of the College Staff - Other (Temporary or Occasional) The OC Head Coach- Mock Trial Program is responsible for organizing and conducting the Mock Trial Program, ensuring compliance with the rules of the AMTA (American Mock Trial Association). \nhttps://www.coloradocollege.edu/other/mock-trial/meet-the-team.html Read more OC Arena Specialist On Campus Athletics Staff - Other (Temporary or Occasional) The Occasional Arena Specialist plays a key role in the daily operations of Ed Robson Arena, ensuring a positive experience for all patrons through exceptional customer service, ticket scanning, and point-of-sale transactions. This position also supports facility upkeep, rentals, and event assistance to maintain a welcoming and well-functioning environment. Read more Displaying all 21 entries Not Able To Find The Right Job? Sign up for job alerts and we'll email you when new jobs are posted! First Name (required) 1059b6e8 Last Name (required) ad1c1d61 Email (required) 8383ed1a Job Alert c6322edb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Employment Type Department Sign Up Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all Equal Opportunity Consistent with its obligations under the law, Colorado College will provide reasonable accommodation to any employee with a disability who requires accommodation to perform the essential functions of the job. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. If you have a disability and would like to request accommodations to support your application or interview process, please contact Human Resources at HR@coloradocollege.edu as early as possible. Positions may close on the listed deadline or, if posted as continuous, may close without prior notice. Categories Accounting Careers Technology Careers Education Careers Administration Careers Recruiting Careers Quick Links About Us Contact Us Contribute Privacy Policy Sitemap Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Colorado College. Colorado College . Please choose a department"
